T282	Cue 27984 27988	said
T284	Quotation 28004 28083	"Madame, you must go at once to Monsieur Homais. It's for something important."
T285	Entity 27724 27727	she
R303	Addressee Arg1:T285 Arg2:T284	
R304	Cueing Arg1:T282 Arg2:T284	
T286	Entity 28977 28987	the chemis
T287	Cue 28989 29002	was screaming
T288	Quotation 29005 29057	"Who told you to go and fetch it in the Capharnaum."
T289	Quotation 29058 29091	"What is it? What is the matter?"
T290	Entity 28933 28939	Justin
T291	Quotation 29092 29105	"What is it?"
T292	Cue 29106 29113	replied
T293	Entity 29114 29126	the druggist
T294	Quotation 29128 29388	"We are making preserves; they are simmering; but they were about to boil over, because there is too much juice, and I ordered another pan. Then he, from indolence, from laziness, went and took, hanging on its nail in my laboratory, the key of the Capharnaum."
T295	Quotation 30248 30685	"Yes, from the Capharnaum! The key that locks up the acids and caustic alkalies! To go and get a spare pan! a pan with a lid! and that I shall perhaps never use! Everything is of importance in the delicate operations of our art! But, devil take it! one must make distinctions, and not employ for almost domestic purposes that which is meant for pharmaceutical! It is as if one were to carve a fowl with a scalpel; as if a magistrate -- "
T296	Quotation 30686 30700	"Now be calm,"
T297	Cue 30701 30705	said
T298	Entity 30706 30719	Madame Homais
T299	Entity 30725 30732	Athalie
T300	Cue 30755 30760	cried
T301	Quotation 30761 30774	"Papa! papa!"
T302	Quotation 30775 30794	"No, let me alone,"
T303	Cue 30795 30802	went on
T304	Entity 30803 30815	the druggist
T305	Quotation 30816 31045	"let me alone, hang it! My word! One might as well set up for a grocer. That's it! go it! respect nothing! break, smash, let loose the leeches, burn the mallow-paste, pickle the gherkins in the window jars, tear up the bandages!"
T306	Quotation 31046 31069	"I thought you had -- "
T307	Cue 31070 31074	said
T308	Entity 31075 31079	Emma
T309	Quotation 31081 31244	"Presently! Do you know to what you exposed yourself? Didn't you see anything in the corner, on the left, on the third shelf? Speak, answer, articulate something."
T310	Quotation 31245 31264	"I-- don't-- know,"
T311	Cue 31265 31274	stammered
T312	Entity 31275 31291	the young fellow
T313	Quotation 31293 31566	"Ah! you don't know! Well, then, I do know! You saw a bottle of blue glass, sealed with yellow wax, that contains a white powder, on which I have even written 'Dangerous!' And do you know what is in it? Arsenic! And you go and touch it! You take a pan that was next to it!"
T314	Quotation 31567 31580	"Next to it!"
T315	Cue 31581 31586	cried
T316	Entity 31587 31600	Madame Homais
T317	Quotation 31622 31664	"Arsenic! You might have poisoned us all."
T318	Quotation 31754 31776	"Or poison a patient!"
T319	Cue 31777 31786	continued
T320	Entity 31787 31799	the druggist
T321	Quotation 31801 32198	"Do you want to see me in the prisoner's dock with criminals, in a court of justice? To see me dragged to the scaffold? Don't you know what care I take in managing things, although I am so thoroughly used to it? Often I am horrified myself when I think of my responsibility; for the Government persecutes us, and the absurd legislation that rules us is a veritable Damocles' sword over our heads."
T322	Cue 32275 32304	went on in breathless phrases
T323	Entity 32262 32274	the druggist
T324	Entity 32199 32203	Emma
T325	Quotation 32307 32779	"That is your return for all the kindness we have shown you! That is how you recompense me for the really paternal care that I lavish on you! For without me where would you be? What would you be doing? Who provides you with food, education, clothes, and all the means of figuring one day with honour in the ranks of society? But you must pull hard at the oar if you're to do that, and get, as, people say, callosities upon your hands. Fabricando fit faber, age quod agis."
T326	Quotation 33172 33578	"I am beginning to repent terribly of having taken you up! I should certainly have done better to have left you to rot in your poverty and the dirt in which you were born. Oh, you'll never be fit for anything but to herd animals with horns! You have no aptitude for science! You hardly know how to stick on a label! And there you are, dwelling with me snug as a parson, living in clover, taking your ease!"
T327	Entity 33159 33161	HE
T328	Cue 33162 33170	WENT ON-
T329	Entity 33600 33613	Madame Homais
T330	Entity 33583 33587	Emma
T331	Quotation 33615 33644	"I was told to come here -- "
T332	Quotation 33645 33659	"Oh, dear me!"
T333	Cue 33660 33671	interrupted
T334	Entity 33672 33686	the good woman
T335	Quotation 33704 33747	"how am I to tell you? It is a misfortune!"
T336	Entity 33748 33751	She
T337	Entity 33770 33782	the druggist
T338	Cue 33787 33797	thundering
T339	Quotation 33800 33845	"Empty it! Clean it! Take it back! Be quick!"
T340	Quotation 34058 34076	"CONJUGAL-- LOVE!"
T341	Entity 34077 34079	he
T342	Cue 34080 34084	said
T343	Quotation 34119 34200	"Ah! very good! very good! very pretty! And illustrations! Oh, this is too much!"
T344	Entity 34201 34214	Madame Homais
T345	Cue 34215 34227	came forward
T346	Quotation 34229 34251	"No, do not touch it!"
T347	Quotation 34297 34314	"Leave the room,"
T348	Entity 34315 34317	he
T349	Cue 34318 34322	said
T350	Quotation 34557 34918	"Have you every vice, then, little wretch? Take care! you are on a downward path. Did not you reflect that this infamous book might fall in the hands of my children, kindle a spark in their minds, tarnish the purity of Athalie, corrupt Napoleon. He is already formed like a man. Are you quite sure, anyhow, that they have not read it? Can you certify to me -- "
T351	Quotation 34919 34937	"But really, sir,"
T352	Cue 34938 34942	said
T353	Entity 34943 34947	Emma
T354	Quotation 34949 34976	"you wished to tell me -- "
T355	Quotation 34977 35023	"Ah, yes! madame. Your father-in-law is dead."
T356	Quotation 35748 36052	"It is not that I entirely disapprove of the work. Its author was a doctor! There are certain scientific points in it that it is not ill a man should know, and I would even venture to say that a man must know. But later-- later! At any rate, not till you are man yourself and your temperament is formed."
T357	Entity 36084 36091	Charles
T358	Cue 36150 36154	said
T359	Entity 36158 36161	her
T360	Quotation 36188 36202	"Ah! my dear!"
T361	Entity 36365 36368	she
T362	Cue 36369 36380	made answer
T363	Quotation 36382 36404	"Yes, I know, I know!"
T364	Entity 37001 37003	he
T365	Cue 37004 37010	sighed
T366	Quotation 37012 37051	"I should have liked to see him again!"
T367	Quotation 37120 37146	"How old was your father?"
T368	Entity 37147 37150	she
T369	Cue 37151 37156	asked
T370	Quotation 37158 37172	"Fifty-eight."
T371	Quotation 37173 37178	"Ah!"
T372	Entity 37224 37226	he
T373	Cue 37227 37232	added
T374	Quotation 37234 37280	"My poor mother! what will become of her now?"
T375	Quotation 37500 37535	"Did you enjoy yourself yesterday?"
T376	Entity 37536 37538	he
T377	Cue 37539 37544	asked
T378	Quotation 37546 37552	"Yes."
T379	Quotation 38493 38526	"Hallo! you've a pretty bouquet,"
T380	Entity 38527 38529	he
T381	Cue 38530 38534	said
T382	Quotation 38576 38582	"Yes,"
T383	Entity 38583 38586	she
T384	Cue 38587 38594	replied
T385	Quotation 38610 38659	"it's a bouquet I bought just now from a beggar."
T386	Quotation 40470 40522	to offer his services "under the sad circumstances."
T387	Entity 40462 40464	He
T388	Cue 40465 40469	came
T389	Entity 40523 40527	Emma
T390	Cue 40528 40536	answered
T391	Quotation 40537 40574	that she thought she could do without
T392	Quotation 40613 40633	"I beg your pardon,"
T393	Entity 40634 40636	he
T394	Cue 40637 40641	said
T395	Quotation 40643 40695	"but I should like to have a private talk with you."
T396	Cue 40696 40715	Then in a low voice
T397	Quotation 40717 40753	"It's about that affair-- you know."
T398	Entity 40754 40761	Charles
T399	Quotation 40785 40806	"Oh, yes! certainly."
T400	Quotation 40850 40877	"Couldn't you, my darling?"
T401	Entity 40926 40933	Charles
T402	Entity 40840 40848	his wife
T403	Cue 40934 40938	said
T404	Entity 40942 40952	his mother
T405	Quotation 40954 41014	"It is nothing particular. No doubt, some household trifle."
T406	Quotation 41567 41600	"And so you're quite well again?"
T407	Entity 41601 41603	he
T408	Entity 41118 41135	Monsieur Lheureux
T409	Cue 41164 41185	began to congratulate
T410	Entity 41186 41190	Emma
T411	Quotation 41191 41209	on the inheritance
T412	Cue 41211 41223	then to talk
T413	Quotation 41224 41356	of indifferent matters, of the espaliers, of the harvest, and of his own health, which was always so-so, always having ups and downs
T414	Cue 41604 41611	went on
T415	Entity 41510 41513	She
T416	Quotation 41613 41723	"Ma foi! I saw your husband in a sad state. He's a good fellow, though we did have a little misunderstanding."
T417	Quotation 41834 41862	"Why, you know well enough,"
T418	Entity 41724 41727	She
T419	Cue 41728 41733	asked
T420	Quotation 41734 41832	what misunderstanding, for Charles had said nothing of the dispute about the goods supplied to her
T421	Cue 41863 41868	cried
T422	Entity 41869 41877	Lheureux
T423	Quotation 41879 41938	"It was about your little fancies-- the travelling trunks."
T424	Entity 42173 42175	he
T425	Cue 42176 42183	went on
T426	Quotation 42186 42268	"We made it up, all the same, and I've come again to propose another arrangement."
T427	Quotation 42449 42659	"And he would do better to give it over to someone else-- to you, for example. With a power of attorney it could be easily managed, and then we (you and I) would have our little business transactions together."
T428	Quotation 42857 43010	"The one you've on is good enough for the house, but you want another for calls. I saw that the very moment that I came in. I've the eye of an American!"
T429	Entity 42727 42735	Lheureux
T430	Cue 42736 42744	declared
